// Built-in types provided by the dyne compiler.
//
// Loaded via include_str! in compile() before user source so user code
// can refer to Option<T> and Result<T, E> without an explicit declaration.
// Per /design-discussion 2026-05-08 (Q4 / Path 2), the hybrid approach
// of declaring built-ins in dyne syntax keeps the compiler self-host
// friendly: the same parser / resolver / type checker machinery handles
// both built-in and user code.
//
// A failure to compile this file is a compile-time bug in dyne itself
// (sema::builtins::load_builtins panics rather than surfacing the
// diagnostics to user code).

enum Option<T>
  Some(T)
  None
end

enum Result<T, E>
  Ok(T)
  Err(E)
end
